    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0656" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119P43/536: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-25T17:00:00-04:00">July 25, 1919—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2634. Your 3227, July 19th, 7 p.m. Mr. Polk has with him individual document of
                    appointment and full power conferring same powers as given commissioners in
                    joint document of November 30th<anchor n="72" xml:id="d298-f1"/> which
                    Department understands still in effect as regards commissioners remaining in
                    Paris.</p>
                <p>Department concurs in your views as to powers Commissioners to sign treaties with
                    Bulgaria and Turkey and regards present powers as sufficient.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
